WEBVTT

00:00:02.650 --> 00:00:04.900
Jail Scaglietti.

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:09.490
A large-scale interdimensional criminal
with an arrest warrant on several worlds.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:20.000
Many video and voice recordings are available,
but he’s never shown himself in public or been captured.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:25.920
He’s toyed with lives to create biological weapons,

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:33.510
committed a terrorist attack on the Bureau’s Surface HQ,
and even awakened an ancient legacy.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:38.430
With the ship of the holy one rising into the sky, we...

00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:05.960
The things that I can do for you and no one else

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:11.660
I honestly feel and wish for those

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:18.380
I am frozen by uncertainties

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:24.620
By the rules I have been relying on

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:30.320
My past embellished with excuses

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:34.520
I want to get over it

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:37.800
Staining the stars in heaven scarlet

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:41.270
Gather the grains of miracles

00:01:41.270 --> 00:01:44.530
Before the still, unseen night

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:47.810
I want to tell you that I am escaping from illusions

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:50.990
The twilight moon calls out to me

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:54.080
Removing my veil of delusions

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:57.290
My hidden, deceitful self

00:01:57.290 --> 00:02:01.170
And took all of my weaknesses

00:02:01.170 --> 00:02:07.630
I don’t want words that seem passionate

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:17.050
The fact that I’m here right now is my truth

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:44.110
The large ship has surfaced from beneath the earth!

00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:46.270
This can’t be! This is...

00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:53.380
Knight Carim, this is what was in your prophecy.

00:02:58.150 --> 00:03:01.110
The dancing dead.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:05.130
The ship returning from
the holy land under the King’s direction.

00:03:05.990 --> 00:03:10.910
From the age of Ancient Belka, the ultimate physical weapon,

00:03:10.910 --> 00:03:13.840
the ship of the holy one that rules heaven and earth,

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:17.430
the <i>Holy King’s Cradle.</i>

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:29.230
This is the situation I wanted to avoid at all costs.

00:03:29.230 --> 00:03:33.360
It’s the Church’s—no, it’s my fault.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:35.650
My interpretation of the prophecy was insufficient.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:38.770
It’s natural to not know the future.

00:03:38.770 --> 00:03:42.110
It’s not your fault or the Church’s, Carim.

00:03:42.110 --> 00:03:44.640
Now, what do we do?

00:03:44.810 --> 00:03:46.530
Hayate, it’s Chrono.

00:03:46.530 --> 00:03:51.960
The Main Office has judged the <i>Cradle</i>
to be an extremely dangerous Lost Logia.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:55.920
The Dimensional Navy is already on the move.

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:58.880
The G.A.S. is helping as well.

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:01.860
Can Riot Force 6 move out?

00:04:01.860 --> 00:04:02.820
Yes.

00:04:06.640 --> 00:04:10.600
The Vessel of the Holy King and the <i>Cradle</i> have stabilized.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:15.100
Quattro and Dieci, switch with me inside the <i>Cradle.</i>

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:16.090
Okay.

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:16.980
Roger.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:21.640
Tre, Sette, and Sein are to guard the Doctor at his lab.

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:22.820
Understood.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:27.110
Nove... you, Deed, and Wendi are to go with Number XIII.

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:29.220
We’re on our way.

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:32.940
The <i>Cradle</i> will continue to rise
to a level where it can strike the surface.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:40.190
If it reaches a point where it can receive
the magic of the two moons and attack the surface,

00:04:40.190 --> 00:04:43.090
the <i>Cradle</i> will truly be invincible.

00:04:43.910 --> 00:04:46.550
Everyone on Mid will be our hostages.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:50.780
If that’s our position, then we can even deal with the Main Office’s fleet.

00:04:50.780 --> 00:04:53.530
I do have one question, though.

00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:54.480
What?

00:04:54.480 --> 00:05:00.630
That Vessel of the Holy King inside the <i>Cradle,</i> who is she?

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:03.400
I’ll tell you.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:04.770
Doctor.

00:05:04.770 --> 00:05:08.510
It was ten years ago.

00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:12.290
There was a certain priest in the Church of the Holy King.

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:17.250
He was a devout, noble, and kind man.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:22.170
Thus, he earned the position of curator of the holy relics.

00:05:22.170 --> 00:05:23.890
Holy relics?

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:29.860
The bones and possessions of the Holy King,
the sacred ruler of Ancient Belka,

00:05:29.860 --> 00:05:34.080
who is the focus of worship of the Church of the Holy King.

00:05:35.940 --> 00:05:45.000
But even if he was a priest, he was human.
His love for a woman made him take the remains.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:54.080
The genetic data from the small amount
of blood left in the Holy Shroud was removed,

00:05:54.080 --> 00:06:00.540
giving us the genetic data of
the grand ruler of ancient Belka, the Holy King.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:03.140
And the seed of the Holy King was duplicated in secret

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:08.310
in a number of research facilities all around the dimensions, and it awaited rebirth.

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:12.110
To be our king, right?

00:06:12.110 --> 00:06:16.850
A living, breathing Holy King is the key to turn on the <i>Cradle.</i>

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:19.680
It’s a king, but just a tool.

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:22.030
Hey, Doctor, question.

00:06:22.030 --> 00:06:23.520
Go ahead, Sein.

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:26.860
Besides old man Regius,

00:06:26.860 --> 00:06:30.220
is the High Council okay?

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:36.550
They were the ones who sponsored the Artificial Mage Project and the mass-production of the Gadgets, right?

00:06:36.550 --> 00:06:38.100
Yeah, that’s right.

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:43.000
And Miss Lu and Mr. Zest
were revived thanks to them, right?

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:47.970
You don’t think they had a plan
or something of their own, do you?

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:52.530
Regius and the High Council both have the same hope.

00:06:52.530 --> 00:06:56.070
The peace and security of Midchilda and every dimension.

00:06:56.070 --> 00:07:01.810
For that reason, Regius remained obsessed with the discarded combat cyborg plan,

00:07:01.810 --> 00:07:07.010
and the High Council with the Relic weapons
and Artificial Mage Project.

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:18.200
They’re shouldering a rather huge contradiction:
they’re willing to sacrifice innocents to maintain the peace.

00:07:18.200 --> 00:07:21.490
Well, I don’t really get it.

00:07:21.490 --> 00:07:22.450
Yeah.

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:23.420
Anyway,

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:29.570
because they’re our sponsors,
and we ignored them in calling up that huge <i>Cradle,</i>

00:07:29.570 --> 00:07:32.580
I’m worried that they’ll get mad at us.

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:36.260
I’ve made sure they won’t.

00:07:36.260 --> 00:07:41.460
Don’t worry about a thing. Go have fun.

00:07:41.460 --> 00:07:46.510
When you’re done playing,
come back to our new home, the <i>Cradle.</i>

00:07:46.510 --> 00:07:51.340
If you do, the whole world shall be our playground.

00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:55.700
I don’t really get what the Doctor’s saying, as usual.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:57.450
I agree.

00:07:57.450 --> 00:08:01.520
Well, we don’t really have any hopes or dreams.

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:04.690
We’ve just gotta do what Uno says.

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:05.810
That’s right.

00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:10.260
Now that I think about it,
there’s one more thing I don’t understand.

00:08:10.260 --> 00:08:16.200
The woman who made that priest steal the relics of the Holy King...

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:21.580
...was who?

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:28.500
Jail has overdone it.

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:33.900
Even Regius is an important pawn to us.

00:08:33.900 --> 00:08:40.330
And he is trying to make the <i>Holy King’s Cradle</i>
we sought into his own toy.

00:08:40.330 --> 00:08:42.900
We must stop him.

00:08:43.780 --> 00:08:49.150
But Jail is a valuable individual.
It’s a shame to eliminate him so early.

00:08:49.150 --> 00:08:53.240
But Zest of the Artificial Mage Project failed.

00:08:53.240 --> 00:09:00.460
And while Lutecia was also incomplete,
it seems the Vessel of the Holy King is a perfect success.

00:09:00.460 --> 00:09:03.340
Is it not time, perhaps?

00:09:03.340 --> 00:09:07.890
What we seek is a world ruled by a great leader.

00:09:07.890 --> 00:09:14.430
We must pick that leader
and rule the world from the shadows.

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:17.250
That’s why we developed the life-extension technology.

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:19.070
That’s why we have the <i>Cradle.</i>

00:09:19.070 --> 00:09:22.860
We have lived many years watching over the world

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:27.540
by abandoning our bodies, ever since
the olden days, but we won’t last much longer.

00:09:27.540 --> 00:09:33.180
But we must still protect
the Dimensional Sea and the Bureau.

00:09:33.870 --> 00:09:35.970
Excuse me.

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:41.890
If only Zest were in perfect health,
he would’ve been the perfect keeper for Jail.

00:09:41.890 --> 00:09:46.000
Everyone, it’s time for your auto-maintenance.

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:47.810
Oh, it’s you.

00:09:47.810 --> 00:09:49.630
We’re in a conference.

00:09:49.630 --> 00:09:51.550
Be quick about it.

00:09:51.550 --> 00:09:52.270
Yes, sir.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:54.680
He is a warrior.

00:09:54.680 --> 00:09:57.140
We can’t control him.

00:09:57.140 --> 00:10:02.140
By feeding him information on
the combat cyborg plans and guaranteeing Lutecia’s safety,

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:04.700
we’re barely managing to chain him.

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:09.200
If he reaches Regius, it ends there.

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:11.670
You seem worried.

00:10:11.670 --> 00:10:14.590
No, it’s nothing important.

00:10:14.590 --> 00:10:17.550
It’s nothing you must worry about.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:18.830
Yes, sir.

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:22.500
Has there been no contact from Regius or the G.A.S.?

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:25.380
No, nobody’s contacted us yet.

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:26.480
I see.

00:10:26.480 --> 00:10:29.510
It’s going to be busy soon.

00:10:29.510 --> 00:10:31.850
We’ll need you to work as well.

00:10:31.850 --> 00:10:32.710
No.

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:37.860
I’m here because I want to be.

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:45.470
In the old era, it was the three members of the High Council who brought the separated worlds together.

00:10:45.470 --> 00:10:51.170
Even after they entrusted the leadership to us and the Time-Space Administrative Bureau’s system,

00:10:51.170 --> 00:10:54.600
they created the Council System and watched over us.

00:10:54.600 --> 00:11:04.710
Young Reggie—Lt. General Regius—is a bit violent occasionally, but he’s kept the peace on the surface.

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:11.950
So I don’t want to believe they’re involved in this matter.

00:11:14.220 --> 00:11:23.310
Whatever the reason, the High Council and Lt. General Regius tried to use Jail Scaglietti, the brilliant criminal,

00:11:23.310 --> 00:11:27.040
but they ended up being used instead and were betrayed.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:32.440
I don’t know how much was
whose plan, or who was behind what,

00:11:32.440 --> 00:11:38.360
but now the massive ship in the sky,
the combat cyborgs, and the Gadgets have appeared,

00:11:38.360 --> 00:11:40.990
threatening the safety of the city.

00:11:40.990 --> 00:11:41.950
Those are the facts.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:46.220
We must stop them.

00:11:47.170 --> 00:11:50.550
The Main Office’s fleet is heading towards the <i>Cradle.</i>

00:11:50.550 --> 00:11:56.170
All other squads are cooperating to
deal with the combat cyborgs and Gadgets.

00:11:56.170 --> 00:12:00.890
But there aren’t many mages who can handle a high-level A.M.F. in battle.

00:12:00.890 --> 00:12:06.620
We will split into three groups and help in all areas.

00:12:10.560 --> 00:12:11.140
Fate?

00:12:12.490 --> 00:12:15.410
Uh...

00:12:15.410 --> 00:12:18.590
You’re in a different group, huh?

00:12:18.590 --> 00:12:24.550
I’m sorry. I can never be with you when it counts.

00:12:24.550 --> 00:12:25.630
It’s not that.

00:12:25.630 --> 00:12:26.880
Fate.

00:12:26.880 --> 00:12:30.020
I’m worried you’re going to face Scaglietti alone.

00:12:30.020 --> 00:12:34.480
I want to leave Signum on the ground in case of emergency.

00:12:34.480 --> 00:12:39.090
Inspector Acous and Sister Schach will be with me, so I won’t be alone.

00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:42.100
Both of you do your best.

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:44.180
Don’t overdo it.

00:12:44.180 --> 00:12:44.990
Yes.

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:47.870
You too, Fate.

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:54.110
That knight and the red girl may show up again.

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:57.710
Zest Grangeitz and his Unight, Agito.

00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:02.670
Major Nakajima told me about Knight Zest.

00:13:02.670 --> 00:13:08.120
He was a striker-tier mage attached to the Bureau’s Capital Defense Corps.

00:13:08.120 --> 00:13:14.000
A good friend of Lt. General Regius who supposedly died eight years ago.

00:13:27.930 --> 00:13:31.640
Three minutes until the Group 1 drop point.

00:13:31.640 --> 00:13:34.820
Three minutes until the Group 1 drop point.

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:39.360
Our mission this time will be harder than ever.

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:44.490
And Nanoha and I won’t be able
to come save you if you’re in trouble.

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:50.180
But close your eyes for a moment,
and remember your training.

00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:55.470
The basic skills that you’ve repeated over and over again.

00:13:55.470 --> 00:13:58.650
Your special skills that you’ve polished and polished.

00:13:58.650 --> 00:14:01.680
The defense training where you were hurt.

00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:05.070
The formations you repeated until your whole body hurt.

00:14:05.070 --> 00:14:08.990
The mock battles you did with us
over and over again until you were barely able to stand.

00:14:12.230 --> 00:14:13.480
You can open your eyes.

00:14:14.940 --> 00:14:18.620
Well, I don’t know if I can say it, but it was tough.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:23.750
You’ve done well to make it this far, the four of you.

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:27.690
“All four of you are stronger than anybody else.”

00:14:27.690 --> 00:14:29.420
I can’t really say that yet.

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:36.180
But I’ve trained you to deal with anybody in any situation.

00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:39.430
The power to protect what you must protect,

00:14:39.430 --> 00:14:42.010
the power to save what you must save,

00:14:42.010 --> 00:14:45.550
and the power to stand up
in the face of a desperate situation.

00:14:45.550 --> 00:14:50.110
After how hard you’ve worked, you have all of those things.

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:54.940
This is what you dreamed and longed for
all those times you did your best together,

00:14:54.940 --> 00:14:58.320
all those times you put all that effort into it
no matter how painful it was.

00:14:58.320 --> 00:15:00.540
They’ve all been worth it.

00:15:01.110 --> 00:15:03.040
Don’t forget that.

00:15:03.040 --> 00:15:07.970
It’s the ability to overcome
a desperate situation that makes a striker.

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:09.680
Yes, ma’am!

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:11.870
Okay, Riot Force 6 forward squad,

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:12.780
move out!

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:14.000
Get going!

00:15:14.000 --> 00:15:14.660
Yes, ma’am!

00:15:20.300 --> 00:15:21.830
I’m going on ahead.

00:15:25.820 --> 00:15:27.340
Subaru.

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:32.160
I know you’re worried about Ginga, and I’m sure—

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:33.820
You’re wrong!

00:15:34.650 --> 00:15:36.900
Ginny is most likely fine.

00:15:36.900 --> 00:15:38.750
I’ll save her for sure.

00:15:39.820 --> 00:15:44.030
For now, Nanoha, I’m worried about you and Vivio.

00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:46.120
Thank you, Subaru.

00:15:46.120 --> 00:15:47.690
But I’m okay.

00:15:48.630 --> 00:15:55.600
The thing I was most afraid of was not being able to go out there, but Commander Yagami gave me the go-ahead.

00:15:55.600 --> 00:16:01.020
If I can go out and do my best,
then there’s nothing I’m worried about.

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:02.840
Vivio will be okay, too.

00:16:02.840 --> 00:16:04.940
I’ll save her.

00:16:04.940 --> 00:16:07.660
So don’t worry.

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:13.820
The Nanoha you’ve always admired
is an invincible ace who won’t lose to anybody, Subaru.

00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:16.280
Yes, ma’am.

00:16:16.280 --> 00:16:20.700
And Subaru, you’re our front attacker,
the pride of our squad.

00:16:20.700 --> 00:16:25.450
Do your best with your partner, Mach Caliber.

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:26.640
Yes, ma’am!

00:16:45.430 --> 00:16:47.920
Just what are you doing crying before a mission?

00:16:48.510 --> 00:16:52.760
I tried to give Nanoha a pep talk.

00:16:52.760 --> 00:16:55.050
And she gave <i>you</i> one instead?

00:16:55.050 --> 00:16:55.860
Yeah.

00:16:55.860 --> 00:17:01.070
You idiot. It’s ten years too early
for you to be doing that to Nanoha.

00:17:01.070 --> 00:17:06.850
If you want to cheer Nanoha on, you need to be far stronger and better than you are now.

00:17:06.850 --> 00:17:07.860
Yeah.

00:17:17.710 --> 00:17:20.060
Okay, Officer Team, you’re up!

00:17:20.060 --> 00:17:21.520
Ma’am!

00:17:24.240 --> 00:17:26.100
Opening bottom hatch!

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:40.470
Ability limiters for Riot Force 6’s captains and lieutenants are now completely released.

00:17:41.790 --> 00:17:48.670
Hayate, Signum, Vita, Nanoha, Fate, everyone, be safe.

00:17:50.130 --> 00:17:51.630
Do your best.

00:17:51.630 --> 00:17:53.510
We’ll handle this as quickly as possible.

00:17:53.510 --> 00:17:55.090
Leave it to us.

00:17:56.550 --> 00:17:58.660
Limit release!

00:18:06.050 --> 00:18:07.220
<b>Exceed</b>

00:18:07.220 --> 00:18:08.010
Drive...

00:18:08.010 --> 00:18:09.440
...Ignition

00:18:19.560 --> 00:18:20.550
Nanoha?

00:18:20.550 --> 00:18:22.010
Fate.

00:18:22.010 --> 00:18:26.570
Nanoha, about your and
Raising Heart’s Limit Break, Blaster Mode...

00:18:26.570 --> 00:18:31.020
I’m sure you won’t listen to me if I tell you not to use it, Nanoha, so I won’t.

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:33.960
But please, don’t overdo it.

00:18:33.960 --> 00:18:36.590
I’m more worried about you, Fate.

00:18:36.590 --> 00:18:39.840
Bardiche’s and your Limit Break
is extremely powerful, Fate,

00:18:39.840 --> 00:18:43.130
but it’s also very dangerous
and puts a lot of stress on you to use.

00:18:43.130 --> 00:18:44.550
I’m fine.

00:18:44.550 --> 00:18:45.540
Don’t worry.

00:18:48.170 --> 00:18:50.670
Fate, you’re being as stubborn as always.

00:18:50.930 --> 00:18:54.650
N-Nanoha, you’re always doing dangerous things!

00:18:54.650 --> 00:18:56.960
I’m an aerial mage.

00:18:56.960 --> 00:18:58.470
Doing dangerous things is my job.

00:18:58.470 --> 00:19:01.460
Even so, you do too much, Nanoha!

00:19:02.440 --> 00:19:03.310
I...

00:19:03.310 --> 00:19:06.520
Do you know how much we’ve worried?

00:19:06.520 --> 00:19:07.240
I do.

00:19:07.870 --> 00:19:11.100
I know very well how much you’ve worried about me.

00:19:12.490 --> 00:19:15.520
So I’ll come back safe today.

00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:18.990
I’ll come back with Vivio, happy and safe.

00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:23.960
Hey, Fate?

00:19:23.960 --> 00:19:24.780
It’s kind of time we...

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:28.830
Don’t overdo it, Captain Fate.

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:32.250
We’ll make sure the land and sky are safe.

00:19:32.250 --> 00:19:34.470
Great! I’ll be all right.

00:19:34.470 --> 00:19:35.890
Good luck.

00:19:35.890 --> 00:19:37.690
Yep, good luck to you too.

00:19:45.980 --> 00:19:51.600
Sad events, unreasonable pain, and unchangeable fate.

00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:58.070
I hated those, and I didn’t want to allow them.
So I wanted the power to break through them.

00:19:58.070 --> 00:19:59.820
I chose this path,

00:20:02.160 --> 00:20:07.920
and I chose the path of sharing my skills and power
with those kids who felt the same way.

00:20:16.630 --> 00:20:20.760
Magic like this is there to protect what means the most to you.

00:20:20.760 --> 00:20:24.090
It’s a power I need to make my wishes come true.

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:42.110
Wait for me, Vivio!

00:20:49.880 --> 00:20:51.390
Welcome back, Uno.

00:20:51.390 --> 00:20:53.370
Thanks.

00:20:53.370 --> 00:20:56.630
Tre, Sein, and Sette are back.

00:20:56.630 --> 00:20:58.770
Counterattack preparations are complete.

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:02.240
Quattro and Dieci are inside the <i>Cradle,</i>

00:21:02.240 --> 00:21:07.160
and my other sisters are heading to
their respective mission points and Surface HQ.

00:21:07.160 --> 00:21:12.500
I asked Lutecia, and she’s going to help us as well.

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:14.860
Knight Zest is on the move, as well.

00:21:14.860 --> 00:21:17.230
If he acts in an unexpected manner—

00:21:17.230 --> 00:21:19.370
It’s not a problem.

00:21:19.370 --> 00:21:24.470
As soon as she completes her present mission,
Due will head for Surface HQ.

00:21:31.840 --> 00:21:34.290
W-Why?

00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:36.670
Why?

00:21:37.690 --> 00:21:41.650
It’s not healthy for you old folks to work so hard.

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:44.610
It’s time for you to say good night.

00:21:44.610 --> 00:21:46.520
You witch! Jail’s...

00:21:47.600 --> 00:21:51.970
The genius that you found, created, and raised.

00:21:51.970 --> 00:21:59.330
With the knowledge of a lost world and
the infinite greed within him, the pride of Alhazred.

00:22:00.150 --> 00:22:01.690
Development codename:

00:22:01.690 --> 00:22:04.460
Unlimited Desire.

00:22:04.460 --> 00:22:06.860
Jail Scaglietti.

00:22:06.860 --> 00:22:13.320
The moment you created him
and gave him power, your fate was sealed.

00:22:13.320 --> 00:22:19.730
No matter what chain you put around his neck,
or what prison you put him in,

00:22:19.730 --> 00:22:24.670
the power you cannot master
will bring about your destruction.

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:31.990
Nonsense! Impossible!

00:22:31.990 --> 00:22:33.600
Good night.

00:22:42.500 --> 00:22:44.920
Mages, group into formation!

00:22:44.920 --> 00:22:47.380
Were going to take out the smaller units!

00:22:50.750 --> 00:22:52.960
Look for a way inside!

00:22:52.960 --> 00:22:54.930
Assault Team, report your position!

00:23:00.970 --> 00:23:03.250
Enemy group 7 destroyed!

00:23:03.250 --> 00:23:04.130
Next!

00:23:04.130 --> 00:23:05.190
Yes, ma’am!

00:23:10.350 --> 00:23:11.280
Mama.

00:23:11.280 --> 00:23:16.660
It will be a little over three hours before the Dimensional Navy reaches their location for the assault on the <i>Cradle</i>.

00:23:16.660 --> 00:23:21.120
We estimate three hours until we reach the orbital point.

00:23:21.120 --> 00:23:23.040
Three hours.

00:25:17.260 --> 00:25:20.700
Lt. Vita and I
infiltrate the Cradle.<i></i>

00:25:20.700 --> 00:25:24.700
Sister Schach and I infiltrate Scaglietti’s hideout.

00:25:24.700 --> 00:25:26.960
And the forwards...

00:25:33.110 --> 00:25:34.660
Take off!
